From 3934bf55013a086f08c1ab41d55b3c0ed8bbc6ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 13:45:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 43/75] wm: launch ARC standalone dialog tasks FULLSCREEN
 (centered modal)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Complements 0042. A standalone dialog task (floating-themed root activity,
e.g. SystemUI WifiDebuggingActivity, permission prompts) launched freeform on
a freeform display: top-aligned at origin (0,0) and shorter than the screen,
so the card — centered within the task — sat too high (vertically off-center).

The SF dialog-centering path (WaylandTaskOutput, commit b37f8bc) only screen-
centers a card whose task footprint is the full display (render target larger
than the card). On r150 Chrome no longer sends an enlarged render target /
geometry for the ARC modal (confirmed on device: no setRenderTargetSize at all
for the dialog task), so a freeform dialog never gets centered.

Force FULLSCREEN windowing mode for container tasks whose root activity uses a
floating theme. WMS then centers the dialog window within the full display, the
1:1 task composition lands it screen-centered, and the input frame stays
aligned (the model PackageInstaller already relies on). Bounds are cleared so
patch 0042's origin-zeroing and applyArcAspectRatio both correctly no-op.

usesFloatingTheme() in ActivityRecord is made package-visible for the check.
The translucent multi-activity dialog case (non-floating root, e.g.
PackageInstaller) is not covered here and stays freeform; 0042 keeps its input
aligned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ifed9fafc076d41f2f0ab83cbedfb2fcb595adda7
---
 .../com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java |  5 +++-
 .../server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java   | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
index a94acd20f222..5d4a12827ed1 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
@@ -7565,7 +7565,10 @@ final class ActivityRecord extends WindowToken implements WindowManagerService.A
     }
 
     /** Whether this activity's theme declares windowIsFloating (dialog theme). */
-    private boolean usesFloatingTheme() {
+    // fydroid-rt: package-visible so TaskLaunchParamsModifier can force a
+    // standalone dialog task to FULLSCREEN (centered modal). See the
+    // container-dialog-fullscreen block there.
+    boolean usesFloatingTheme() {
         if (info == null || info.applicationInfo == null) {
             return false;
         }
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java
index 65aa9083f770..00a3ff45c922 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java
@@ -314,6 +314,33 @@ class TaskLaunchParamsModifier implements LaunchParamsModifier {
         } else {
             if (DEBUG) appendLog("non-freeform-task-display-area");
         }
+        // fydroid-rt: A standalone dialog task (floating-themed root activity,
+        // e.g. SystemUI's WifiDebuggingActivity or a permission prompt) must
+        // present as a screen-centered modal. On a freeform display it would
+        // otherwise launch freeform, top-aligned at origin (0,0) and shorter
+        // than the screen, so the centered-in-task card sits too high. The SF
+        // dialog-centering (WaylandTaskOutput) only screen-centers a card whose
+        // task footprint is the full display; on r150 Chrome sends no enlarged
+        // render target to fake that for a freeform task. Force FULLSCREEN so
+        // WMS centers the card within the full display and the 1:1 task
+        // composition lands it screen-centered with the input frame aligned —
+        // the same model PackageInstaller relies on. This MUST run before the
+        // PHASE_WINDOWING_MODE return below (the windowing mode is consumed
+        // there); bounds are then resolved empty for fullscreen in STEP 4. (The
+        // translucent multi-activity dialog case, where the ROOT activity isn't
+        // floating, is not covered here and stays freeform; patch 0042 keeps its
+        // input aligned.)
+        if (android.os.Build.IS_CONTAINER && root != null
+                && root.usesFloatingTheme()) {
+            launchMode = WINDOWING_MODE_FULLSCREEN;
+            // Drop any freeform bounds inherited from the persister/caller and
+            // un-resolve so STEP 4 recomputes empty (fullscreen) bounds; leaving
+            // stale freeform bounds on a FULLSCREEN task is inconsistent.
+            fullyResolvedCurrentParam = false;
+            outParams.mBounds.setEmpty();
+            if (DEBUG) appendLog("container-dialog-fullscreen");
+        }
+
         // If launch mode matches display windowing mode, let it inherit from display.
         outParams.mWindowingMode = launchMode == suggestedDisplayArea.getWindowingMode()
                 ? WINDOWING_MODE_UNDEFINED : launchMode;
-- 
